    "limitations": [
      "get_variable_defs returns only variables APPLIED to a layer in the queried subtree. Tokens defined in Figma but not yet used anywhere will be absent. The Text Preview section (929:28132) exists to make the typography set exhaustive; the colour/number groups are still subject to this limit. THIS HAS NOW BITTEN ONCE: Surface/Card (#fafafb) was absent from every extraction because no layer used it, which led CLAUDE.md to assert the surface stack was only Frame/Neutral/Paper. The 2026-08-22 Text Input Container update introduced a BG=Neutral variant that applies it, and search_design_system confirmed it as a real variable in Collection 1. Prefer search_design_system over get_variable_defs when auditing whether a token group is complete.",
      "DUPLICATE NAMES SILENTLY DROP STYLES. The response is a keyed object, so two Figma styles sharing a name collapse into one. This happened: two frames were both named 'Label S Sans', and only the JetBrains Mono one survived — so the Inter style was invisible AND the surviving entry's values were attributed to the wrong style. The designer renamed the mono one to 'Label S Mono'. If a style looks wrong, check for a name collision first.",
      "Body & Supporting/Help & Caption is applied to component layers but is absent from the Text Preview section. Retained here rather than dropped; confirm whether it is still current.",
      "The Icon page (66:17) uses no variables and is intentionally not represented here.",
      "Numbers/* duplicates Radius/* and Stroke/* exactly and is treated as a legacy alias set — recorded for provenance, skipped by the generator."
    ],
    "resolved": [
      "lineHeight: the API returns the sentinel 100 for Figma's \"Auto\". It does NOT mean 100%. Verified against the Text Preview section's own meta line, which reads 'Line height: Auto'. Recorded here as the string \"AUTO\" and emitted as CSS line-height: normal, which uses the font's intrinsic metrics (~1.21x for Inter). An earlier extraction wrongly emitted line-height: 1, which was too tight.",
      "letterSpacing: EVERY value this API returns is a PERCENTAGE, not px. Verified from the same meta line ('Letter spacing: 0.4%'). Stored as letterSpacingPercent and emitted as em: 10 -> 0.1em, 0.4 -> 0.004em. An earlier extraction wrongly emitted 0.4px.",
      "textTransform: the six Label styles are marked UPPER in the section. Tailwind's --text-* cannot carry text-transform (or font-family), so the generator emits paired type-label-* utilities that bundle the casing."
    ]
  },
